      ],
      "method": "On the humeral cylinder the latissimus arc changes side where the segment crosses the axis: no length jump but a moment arm step of 12-19 mm, whichever side site. A sphere of the same centre and radius, without side site, has no such step (below 0.5 mm) and leaves the arms in the planes of Ackland et al. 2008 unchanged; the same on both versions. DELT2 stays on the cylinder."
    }
